From 6f56b2d6c4f3b7e5e9980d3d1caa34b1
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: mt6357: allow VAUD28 to settle before component bind

The MT6357 platform probe enables VAUD28 before registering the codec
component. Leave a short settling interval after the regulator has been
enabled so the component (and subsequently the sound card) cannot bind while
the analog supply is still rising.

The interval is intentionally small and uses a sleepable delay: the
dandelion DT describes a 264 us VAUD28 enable ramp, and the MT6768 vendor
codec also inserts 250 us waits in its analog power-up sequence. This does
not replace the runtime DAPM sequencing.

--- a/sound/soc/codecs/mt6357.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/mt6357.c
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
  * Author: Nicolas Belin <nbelin@baylibre.com>
  */
 
+#include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/dma-mapping.h>
 #include <sound/soc.h>
 #include <sound/tlv.h>
@@ -1795,6 +1796,12 @@ static int mt6357_platform_driver_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ret)
 		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, ret, "Failed to enable vaud28 regulator\n");
 
+	/*
+	 * Let the analog supply settle before the codec component can bind.
+	 * The board DT specifies a 264 us VAUD28 enable ramp.
+	 */
+	usleep_range(500, 1000);
+
 	priv = devm_kzalloc_obj(&pdev->dev, *priv);
 	if (!priv)
 		return -ENOMEM;
-- 
